## Summary

This policy favors:

-   preserving normal, intended existing behavior across the supported GNU
    Emacs range, corrected rather than kept when it is a bug
-   deliberate, evidence-based retirement of legacy components over either
    permanent preservation or inference from age
-   incremental evolution, including version-gated new capabilities that are
    not required to run on Emacs versions that predate them
-   operational stability over stylistic modernization
-   published paths and existing names over formal uniformity

Following these principles ensures that Emacs Lisp configurations remain
functional and maintainable across multiple decades of Emacs development,
while still allowing the maintainer to retire what has genuinely earned
retirement.
